<strong>Update – 10:30 a.m. Pacific Time:</strong> <em>CNET</em> has corrected its article and now says only the HomePod mini 2 will support Siri AI. Original article follows.<br/>
<br/>
<hr />Siri AI will apparently not be limited to the new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/apple-homepod-mini-2/">HomePod mini 2</a>, with support also coming to the first-generation HomePod mini in a software update later this year, according to a report today <a href="https://www.cnet.com/home/smart-home/siri-ai-coming-to-older-apple-devices/">from <em>CNET</em>'s Jeff Carlson</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2020/11/homepod-mini-thumb-feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-770560" /><br/>
"The HomePod Mini 2 also gets a faster S10 processor, which should help with processing Siri AI requests," he said. "However, the current S5-powered HomePod Mini will also get Siri AI compatibility later this year, along with updates to iOS 27.2."<br/>
<br/>
Fine print on Apple's website does not mention this detail, at least as far as we have seen, so we have reached out to the company for comment.<br/>
<br/>
For the Apple TV 4K, Apple's fine print did mention that Siri AI support will <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/older-apple-tv-4k-models-apple-intelligence/">extend back to the second-generation Apple TV 4K</a> from 2021, but we have not found any explicit fine print mention about Siri AI coming to the HomePod mini (1st generation).<br/>
<br/>
Apple said setting up Siri AI on the HomePod mini 2 will require a paired iPhone or iPad model with Apple Intelligence support.<br/>
<br/>
A paired device iPhone or iPad with Apple Intelligence support is also required for any requests involving a user's personal context, according to Apple. However, once Siri AI is enabled on the HomePod mini, the company said that even users without an Apple Intelligence-enabled iPhone or iPad can access Siri AI's broad world knowledge, richer and more natural conversations, and improved music discovery.<br/>
<br/>
